sprdwcn: mbuf_pool_deinit() on a channel without a pool does nothing

Same fix as upstream/modules/wcn_bsp: the Wi-Fi post-init error path deinitialises the channel that failed. When
its EDMA init failed after an earlier power cycle, its pool has no memory (freed then) but keeps that cycle's size,
and the memset of NULL oopsed.

--- a/drivers/unisoc_platform/sprdwcn/pcie/mchn.c
+++ b/drivers/unisoc_platform/sprdwcn/pcie/mchn.c
@@ -140,6 +140,9 @@
 
 int mbuf_pool_deinit(struct buffer_pool *pool)
 {
+	/* MU300: a channel whose EDMA init failed has no pool this time (its size is still the last one's) */
+	if (!pool->mem)
+		return 0;
 	memset(pool->mem, 0x00, (sizeof(struct mbuf_t) +
 	       pool->payload) * pool->size);
 	kfree(pool->mem);
